{"content_hash": "0226612795887e50", "version_id": 573, "article_id": 58, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Nikon strips prize from AI-generated microscope video", "title_zh": "尼康撤销AI生成的显微视频奖项", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "bbc_tech", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr86z33pdy9vo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1614036417651-efe5912149d8?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cHJpemUlMjB3aW5uaW5nJTIwaW1hZ2V8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc5MTc2NTYxNXww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Brands&People on Unsplash", "author": "Brands&People", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@brandsandpeople?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/yellow-paper-award-ribbon-ZdqSuxl3Lak?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(16, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(54, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "cec84960fed8"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 163, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "Nikon has taken back a top prize from a science video contest. The company found that the winning video was made with generative AI, which is against the rules.", "lead_zh": "尼康撤销了一项科学视频比赛的大奖。公司发现获奖视频是用生成式AI制作的，这违反了比赛规则。", "preview": "Nikon said the video broke the rules of its Small World In Motion contest, which is for images taken with powerful microscopes. The contest ", "preview_zh": "尼康表示，该视频违反了其“运动中的微观世界”比赛规则，该比赛面向用高倍显微镜拍摄的图像。比赛已举办15年。尼康在重新检查视频并咨询评委后做出了这一决定。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 562, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/58/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 66.088, "size_bytes": 400320, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 181, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@870ce8b/content/data/versions/573.json", "paragraphs": ["Nikon said the video broke the rules of its Small World In Motion contest, which is for images taken with powerful microscopes. The contest has run for 15 years. Nikon made the decision after re-checking the video and talking to its judges.", "The winner was Dr Ning Xu from Tsinghua University in China. His video showed tiny hair-like structures called cilia moving in the airway of a child with PCD, a breathing condition. Xu had said he used AI but believed he followed the rules.", "Several scientists, including former judges, complained on LinkedIn that the video looked fake. Dr Robert Hirst from the University of Leicester said he was not surprised and knew immediately it was fabricated. He has diagnosed PCD for 20 years.", "Hirst added that the cells and cilia did not look like those from real PCD patients. He said the controversy has affected many patients, scientists, doctors and support networks worldwide. Nikon will now review the contest's rules and procedures."], "paragraphs_zh": ["尼康表示，该视频违反了其“运动中的微观世界”比赛规则，该比赛面向用高倍显微镜拍摄的图像。比赛已举办15年。尼康在重新检查视频并咨询评委后做出了这一决定。", "获奖者是来自中国清华大学的徐宁博士。他的视频展示了名为纤毛的微小毛发状结构在患有PCD（一种呼吸系统疾病）的儿童气道中移动。徐曾表示他使用了AI，但认为遵守了规则。", "几位科学家，包括前评委，在领英上投诉称该视频看起来是假的。莱斯特大学的罗伯特·赫斯特博士表示他并不惊讶，并立即知道视频是伪造的。他诊断PCD已有20年。", "赫斯特补充说，细胞和纤毛看起来不像真实PCD患者的。他说这场争议影响了全球许多患者、科学家、医生和支持网络。尼康现在将审查比赛的规则和程序。"], "body": "Nikon said the video broke the rules of its Small World In Motion contest, which is for images taken with powerful microscopes. The contest has run for 15 years. Nikon made the decision after re-checking the video and talking to its judges.\n\nThe winner was Dr Ning Xu from Tsinghua University in China. His video showed tiny hair-like structures called cilia moving in the airway of a child with PCD, a breathing condition. Xu had said he used AI but believed he followed the rules.\n\nSeveral scientists, including former judges, complained on LinkedIn that the video looked fake. Dr Robert Hirst from the University of Leicester said he was not surprised and knew immediately it was fabricated. He has diagnosed PCD for 20 years.\n\nHirst added that the cells and cilia did not look like those from real PCD patients. He said the controversy has affected many patients, scientists, doctors and support networks worldwide. Nikon will now review the contest's rules and procedures.", "body_zh": "尼康表示，该视频违反了其“运动中的微观世界”比赛规则，该比赛面向用高倍显微镜拍摄的图像。比赛已举办15年。尼康在重新检查视频并咨询评委后做出了这一决定。\n\n获奖者是来自中国清华大学的徐宁博士。他的视频展示了名为纤毛的微小毛发状结构在患有PCD（一种呼吸系统疾病）的儿童气道中移动。徐曾表示他使用了AI，但认为遵守了规则。\n\n几位科学家，包括前评委，在领英上投诉称该视频看起来是假的。莱斯特大学的罗伯特·赫斯特博士表示他并不惊讶，并立即知道视频是伪造的。他诊断PCD已有20年。\n\n赫斯特补充说，细胞和纤毛看起来不像真实PCD患者的。他说这场争议影响了全球许多患者、科学家、医生和支持网络。尼康现在将审查比赛的规则和程序。", "text": "Nikon said the video broke the rules of its Small World In Motion contest, which is for images taken with powerful microscopes. The contest has run for 15 years. Nikon made the decision after re-checking the video and talking to its judges. The winner was Dr Ning Xu from Tsinghua University in China. His video showed tiny hair-like structures called cilia moving in the airway of a child with PCD, a breathing condition. Xu had said he used AI but believed he followed the rules. Several scientists, including former judges, complained on LinkedIn that the video looked fake. Dr Robert Hirst from the University of Leicester said he was not surprised and knew immediately it was fabricated. He has diagnosed PCD for 20 years. Hirst added that the cells and cilia did not look like those from real PCD patients. He said the controversy has affected many patients, scientists, doctors and support networks worldwide. Nikon will now review the contest's rules and procedures.", "vocab": [{"word": "disqualify", "pos": "verb", "zh": "取消资格", "note": "常用被动语态：be disqualified from", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "generative AI", "pos": "noun", "zh": "生成式人工智能", "note": "指能生成文本、图像等的AI", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "microscope", "pos": "noun", "zh": "显微镜", "note": "科学仪器", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "contest", "pos": "noun", "zh": "比赛", "note": "同competition", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "complaint", "pos": "noun", "zh": "投诉", "note": "动词complain", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "fabricated", "pos": "adj", "zh": "伪造的", "note": "动词fabricate", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "diagnose", "pos": "verb", "zh": "诊断", "note": "医疗用语", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "controversy", "pos": "noun", "zh": "争议", "note": "常与spark/arouse连用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "review", "pos": "verb", "zh": "审查", "note": "此处指重新检查", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "procedure", "pos": "noun", "zh": "程序", "note": "常用复数procedures", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Prize-winning image which sparked backlash was AI-generated, Nikon rules", "summary_original": "The camera-maker says it is now re-evaluating the rules and procedures of its Small World in Motion contest.", "body_original": "Prize-winning image which sparked backlash was AI-generated, Nikon rules\nBy\nZoe Kleinman\nTechnology & AI editor\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nThe winner of a prestigious scientific photography competition has been disqualified following concerns raised by other scientists that it was fake.\nNikon said the use of generative AI in the composition of the video broke the rules of its Small World In Motion contest, which accepts photos and video taken using powerful microscopes.\nThe firm said the video \"did not comply with the competition rules regarding generative AI\", but added it was not a judgement of the entrant's professional reputation or scientific contributions.\nIt said it would now look at the rules and procedures of the annual contest, which has been running for 15 years and is specifically for microscopic images.\nNikon said it came to the decision \"after thoroughly re-evaluating the video and supporting materials and consulting with members of our judging panel\".\nThe winning entry came from Dr Ning Xu, from Tsinghua University in China, who submitted a short video showing tiny, hair-like structures called cilia moving in the airway of a child with the respiratory condition PCD.\nThe BBC has approached him for comment.\nA number of scientists, including former competition judges, complained to Nikon on its LinkedIn page that the video did not appear to be real.\nXu had acknowledged using AI, but said he believed he had acted within the rules, and had cooperated with Nikon's investigation.\nUniversity of Leicester scientist Dr Robert Hirst, who was among the first experts to voice concerns, said he was \"not surprised\" and he \"knew immediately that the video was fabricated\".\n\"I have been diagnosing PCD for 20 years by examining their cilia waveform, length, cell size and shape,\" he said.\nHirst, who is lead scientist for the NHS centre for PCD diagnosis at the university, said the cells and cilia \"look nothing like those from PCD patients\".\n\"This controversy has impacted a lot of patients, scientists, doctors and PCD support networks around the world,\" he said.\nTiny image sparks big backlash in Nikon photo contest\nPublished\n1 October\nWhat is AI, how does it work and why are some people concerned about it?\nPublished\n14 September\nSign up for our Tech Decoded newsletter\nto follow the world's top tech stories and trends.\nOutside the UK? Sign up here\n.\nRelated topics\nArtificial intelligence\nPhotography\nScience & Environment", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:40:13.616651", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Nikon", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.688, "sm": 100, "em": 687, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "said", "s": 0.7, "e": 0.925, "sm": 700, "em": 924, "cs": 6, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "the", "s": 0.938, "e": 1.025, "sm": 937, "em": 1025, "cs": 11, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "video", "s": 1.038, "e": 1.4, "sm": 1037, "em": 1400, "cs": 15, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "broke", "s": 1.413, "e": 1.7, "sm": 1412, "em": 1700, "cs": 21, "